{
  "_doc": "Tier-2 pool building (random towns, civic or commercial lots): a small AM station with its broadcast booth, equipment room and generator shed, and a square lattice mast with two rest platforms under the relay platform. The generator still runs at dusk: the ON AIR sign, the racks and the mast's beacon burn (prop lights on 'generator' power, ADR-0023). Route: the front door is chained -> the yard and the generator shed -> round the back to the hole Bud cut for the generator cable (jaws set in the gap) -> the equipment room -> Bud's office and his log -> the hall, where the boards groan and the ON AIR light burns over the studio door (opening it, or the boards, wakes the booth: ambush) -> the booth: Mel at the console, the Cordon's transcripts -> reception -> back through the office and out of its bolted side door into the mast compound -> up the mast's ladders platform by platform -> the top platform: the relay cabinet (loot) and Bud (guardian) -> back down. Hollowed don't climb ladders: once the top is cleared the mast is a refuge. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
