      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "KHLW 1340 played the farm report and the high-school games until the Cordon took the station over to read its emergency instructions on the hour: boil your water, go to the assembly points, buses at first light. The buses never came, and Lieutenant Voss left on the ninth morning. Mel Ostrander, the night man, kept reading the bulletins into the microphone because somebody out there still had a radio, and Bud Kearney, the engineer, put the generator on a timer, cut a hole through the equipment room's back wall when the conduit was crushed, and locked the Cordon's emergency kit in the relay cabinet on the mast's top platform. Mel would not come out of the booth and kept the ON AIR light burning for company. Bud was bitten fixing the beacon and climbed up one last time to fix the relay. At dusk the generator still turns over, the ON AIR sign glows red over the studio door and the beacon burns on top of the mast for anyone left to see it.",
